No, because factor models are indeterminate. A common factor is not a sum of its indicators, but rather a weighted sum of the mode's observed variables plus an arbitrary component. Moreover, the "1" loadings in your syntax do not mean that the indicators load perfectly on the common factor. If you use the "lavaan()" function, you will be forced to see more of the machinery behind the factor model.

If you want to create a sum, do it outside of lavaan.

--Ed Rigdon

