Are you using the default std.lv <http://std.lv>=FALSE, in which case the first item's loading is fixed to (positive) 1?  The solutions with signs switched are statistically equivalent, changing only the interpretation (direction) of the latent scale.  But you can either fix the first loading to -1 in the syntax, or you can set std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE to estimate all loadings and label the first loading, constraining that label to be < 0 to obtain a comparable solution to your IRT result.

http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html

