> How can I interpret the threshold coefficient of a 0-1 binary endogenous variable in lavaan? Is it the intercept of the probit regression?

No, it is -1 times the intercept, if the intercept were estimated and threshold fixed to zero (instead of vice versa, the default).

It is the value of the "latent item-response" above which respondents respond 1, but below which respondents respond 0.

https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf

https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406

