>

> #Trying to run my SEM model through the weight variable
> survey.fit <-lavaan.survey(fit,
>                            survey.design = "svy.df",
>                            estimator="MLMV")

You cannot use robust ML estimation with ordered outcomes in lavaan (pairwise ML is available, but no robust version of that is available, and it does not work in combination with sampling weights); the default is WLSMV.  The survey package does not provide the functionality necessary for lavaan.survey to be able to accommodate ordered outcomes.  lavaan has its own sampling.weights argument now, but it only works with ML(R) estimator, so it cannot yet accommodate ordered outcomes.

