You can solve that problem by dividing (ormultipying) some of your observed variables by some constant, like a suitable power of 10. Dividing by a constant does not complicate sttistical distributions, like dividing by a sample-based quantity does. Look at the variances of your observed variables, and remember that dividing the raw score by X divides the variance by X squared.

